      608.17,
      539.9,
      631.24
    ],
    "text": "1. A person who wishes to import liquor shall submit an application form set out in accordance with the ScheduleI to the Commissioner General of Excise.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      644.17,
      539.91,
      667.24
    ],
    "text": "2. If the Commissioner General of Excise is satisfied about the application forwarded by the applicant, theapproval shall be sent to the Controller of Imports and Exports with the form set out in accordance with the Schedule II.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      680.17,
      539.87,
      703.24
    ],
    "text": "3. If Commissioner General of Excise is not satisfied about the application, such Commissioner shall inform theapplicant, reason for rejection within five days of the receipt of the application.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
